{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1520820-favorite-immortal","id":1520820,"title":"Favorite Immortal","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-17T08:28:19-07:00","id":1520820,"title":"Favorite Immortal","content":"I'm curious, what is your favorite immortal type and why? (Not counting the Arisen themselves.) I really like body thieves and the purified, I think they can both make great enemies outside of Mummy as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T11:29:50-07:00","id":1520827,"title":"","content":"Purified, but not as presented in immortals (not sure what the 2e treatment is like), as loners and rare, unusual individuals.<br /> <br /> As families, only 'purifying' new members (if at all) after they have produced the next generation - or if the ritual is particularly risky on their deathbeds - though the risk is minimised by repeated attempts, and the scale at which these families operate.<br /> <br /> These families would act as partly patriarchal/matriarchal organisations, part ancestor worship Cult, part corporations adopting new members into the family, depending on the particular group and their founders.<br /> <br /> They might compete with vampires (in an Immortal power game, reminiscent of VtM) but more likely have deals with the forsaken. Learning how to do rituals, sharing knowledge of spirits, and likely getting into conflict with some particularly forsaken pack who decide they should not be allowed to exist (being a mixture of spirit/human, which the forsaken typically think want to keep seperate). I don't know about pack totems, and whether they would need one or gain what they need for the head of the family to be one...<br /> <br /> I think there is room for an entire game there, mortal sorcerers recruited over the years, centuries of occult knowledge accumulated in some libraries, maybe some ghosts (of those who died in the purification gone wrong) left behind are kept well protected and remembered and safely anchored where they are most needed...<br /> <br /> Cross-overs with Mage Liches, Mummys, werewolves, Sin-eaters, and vampires. Oh my.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-30-2024, 10:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T17:13:10-07:00","id":1520847,"title":"","content":"Another vote for the Purified. Blood Bathers would come in second.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T01:39:23-07:00","id":1520859,"title":"","content":"As written, i like the reborn.<br /> <br /> I wonder about them leaving ghosts, or not passing on? I think whatever the answer is, having them interact with the ghost of their former self would be cool - or even being possessed by it. Or learning some necromancy to have a more balanced relationship...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T13:27:10-07:00","id":1521059,"title":"","content":"I also like the Reborn. I think actually being one would be stressful, because most of them have to solve a puzzle from their previous lives to remember how to do the thing that lets them reincarnate, and there's probably no way to know you've done it right until you, y'know, actually die and reincarnate. But they're interesting characters, and possibly the best fit for an Assassin's Creed style protagonist. I also really like the idea of the Wardens; and thought that, say, the Warden of the Spanish Main would be a cool immortal character. Or the Warden of a particular (old) city would be an awesome local contact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T18:09:26-07:00","id":1521230,"title":"","content":"I finally got sold on the Purified with their 2E version, so, uh, them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T12:42:59-07:00","id":1521271,"title":"","content":"I had a fondness for The Purified &amp; the Harvesters group of Immortals and a sick appreciation for the Blood Bathers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-27T14:25:15-07:00","id":1521480,"title":"","content":"Eternals and Purified are my top two! Great as either protagonists or antagonists. I like the parallel nature of immortals whose soul are bound in an item to make the body eternal and those whose soul is bound to the spirit world and their own flesh to become immortal.<br /> <br /> I'd love to play either in a Chronicle!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-27T15:24:46-07:00","id":1521481,"title":"","content":"Purified are my favorites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-27T16:58:45-07:00","id":1521484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1520820-favorite-immortal?p=1521230#post1521230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I finally got sold on the Purified with their 2E version, so, uh, them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where can I find the 2e version of the Purified? I can't seem to find them in Mummy, but I might've just missed it as I haven't read the whole book yet. Purified are my favorites as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1494-deranged-goblin","name":"Deranged Goblin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-27T17:10:57-07:00","id":1521486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deranged Goblin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1520820-favorite-immortal?p=1521484#post1521484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where can I find the 2e version of the Purified? I can't seem to find them in Mummy, but I might've just missed it as I haven't read the whole book yet. Purified are my favorites as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>They got an update along with the Visitors and the Patchwork People in the <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/406043/The-Book-of-Lasting-Death\" target=\"_blank\">Book of Lasting Death</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T19:23:20-07:00","id":1521934,"title":"","content":"Patchwork People for me, especially regarding the implications and possibility of those alchemical Sekhem pumps that that take place of their hearts. If that arcane technology is able to be steadily produced- and it seems to be, if only in very small quantities- I could see a very interesting partnership between an ambitious cult and a conclave of the Elite, figuring out a way to manufacture those pacemakers could be a way to create incentive for loyal service within the cult.. so long as the Patchwork People were properly compensated. Those Specialists seem to be pretty damn invaluable too, that surgical and reconstructive knowledge could be veery useful for certain enterprises.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-10T14:21:33-07:00","id":1522362,"title":"","content":"Purified are my favorite, with second place going to the Harvesters and third to the Visitors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-10T15:04:03-07:00","id":1522363,"title":"","content":"I think the Purified have a great balance of useful powers mixed with the ever looming risk of being a snack to a spirit. They are great for NPCs. How they got their ritual and the components in itself can tell a story, as well as what made them want to take the risks on board or what placed in the right situation for it to happen spontaneously.<br /> <br /> Second favorite are the Blood Bathers, who epitomize the &quot;power at a price&quot; aspect of immortality. The more perks they get, the more hoops they need to jump through. They may become a future Geist as they try to cling to life, they may inspire the Legend of a Slasher, so they are antagonists with a far reaching legacy.<br /> <br /> Third favorite are the Psychic Vampires. They are on a time limit, needing to harness ever more Essence as the years go by, being able to burn through resources quickly. They can be mistaken for vampires because they can manipulate minds and cause damage while feeding. They can be mistaken for changelings because they can feed on will (rather than emotions) and the ones with Soul Eater can be mistaken for Eaters of the Dead.<br /> <br /> In short, I like the balance between risk and reward of the Purified and my other favorites are the ones with powers that push them to cross paths with the players.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-10T16:55:27-07:00","id":1522369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1520820-favorite-immortal?p=1522363#post1522363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third favorite are the Psychic Vampires. They are on a time limit, needing to harness ever more Essence as the years go by, being able to burn through resources quickly. They can be mistaken for vampires because they can manipulate minds and cause damage while feeding. They can be mistaken for changelings because they can feed on will (rather than emotions) and the ones with Soul Eater can be mistaken for Eaters of the Dead.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Psychic Vampires are among my favorite things in CofD, the ability to make someone's vice &quot;obey me&quot; is just so wonderful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}